==English==

===Etymology===
From Greek [[διοπτρικός]]. Compare [[diopter]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/daɪˈɒptɹɪk/}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Acting as a medium for sight; making use of refraction (of lenses, etc.).
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} Pertaining to a [[diopter]].
#* {{quote-book|1=en|year=2014|author=w:Umberto Eco|title=Island of the Day Before|page=363|location=London|publisher=Vintage Books|passage=[W]ould the new Narcissus—without any '''dioptric''' or sciatherical computing—grasp the alternating skirmish of light and shadow.}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} Capable of being seen through.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|in the plural}} The branch of [[optics]] concerned with [[refraction]].
# A dioptric [[telescope]].

